<title>POLAND: POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES UP TO $19.688 BLN IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES UP TO $19.688 BLN IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish official foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves grew by $776 million in June to $19.688 billion and</p>
<p>were $2.048 billion higher than in June 1996, the National Bank</p>
<p>of Poland said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said official reserves grew $1.655 billion in the first</p>
<p>six months of 1997 compared to a $2.677 billion rise in the</p>
<p>corresponding period of last year.</p>
<p> POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  JUNE     MAY	JUNE '96</p>
<p> Official reserves	    19.688   18.912    17.640</p>
<p> Net reserves		   22.654   21.713    21.542</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are</p>
<p>those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of</p>
<p>hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
